WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.590
Posts come in different shapes.

2
00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.769
A square is one to one.

3
00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.615
A vertical story is nine to sixteen.

4
00:00:04.615 --> 00:00:06.308
A wide banner is sixteen to nine.

5
00:00:06.308 --> 00:00:08.000
Your words have to fit all three.

6
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.761
If you stretch the square version to fill the wide banner, the letters get squashed.

7
00:00:11.761 --> 00:00:17.000
Instead re-lay it out: move and resize the words for the wide shape and keep the letters at their normal proportions.

8
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.952
On a vertical story, apps place buttons and captions over the top and bottom edges.

9
00:00:20.952 --> 00:00:25.000
Keep your important words in the middle, inside the safe zone, so nothing is covered.

10
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.150
Keep the timing identical in every format: the same delay between letters, the same easing and the same rest time per word.

11
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.000
That is what makes three layouts feel like one animation.

12
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.264
Finally shrink all three and look at them together.

13
00:00:37.264 --> 00:00:42.000
The words should still read in each one, and they should look like family.
